          "text": "Short answer: it depends on what you need (lowest price, biggest cartons, branded lollies, or a huge selection). Here are the best Australian online options by use-case, with quick pros/cons and sources so you can check stock/prices.\n\n- Cheapest for bulk/brand-name party packs (good if you have a membership): Costco Australia — big, low-cost multipacks and 1–10+ kg party bags (membership/warehouse-delivery rules apply). Example: Skittles 60-pack / 900 g listed at about $38.98. ([costco.com.au](https://www.costco.com.au/SKITTLES/Skittles-Variety-Pack-60-Pack-900g/p/93134_BD?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Best all-round selection (wide range of sweets, single-SKU bulk and small bulk, easy site search): Goody Goody Gum Drops — long-running Aussie online lolly shop with many bulk options. Good for nostalgic or branded lollies. ([goodygoodygumdrops.com.au](https://www.goodygoodygumdrops.com.au/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Excellent variety + party / candy-bar fulfilment (party favours, curated mixes): Lolly Warehouse / Candy Store — big catalogue and ready-made party mixes. Good if you need themed packs or to sort by colour/flavour. ([lollywarehouse.com.au](https://www.lollywarehouse.com.au/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Good for large wholesale cartons and very large-volume orders (10 kg cartons, wholesale-focused lines): Wallies / Lolly.com — sells 10 kg cartons and wholesale-sized lots for events and retailers. ([lolly.com.au](https://www.lolly.com.au/jubes-in-10kg-carton?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Best for wholesale / business / fundraising orders (trade pricing, B2B service): SweetsWorld / other confectionery wholesalers (The Professors, Global Confectionery) — set up a wholesale account for tiered pricing and faster dispatch for big orders. ([sweetsworld.com.au](https://sweetsworld.com.au/wholesale-candy-australia/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- Good value for party-supplies + mix-and-match bulk lollies: Discount Party Warehouse and Sweet As — handy if you want pre-mixed packs, bulk 1 kg bags, and party-stuff in the same order. ([discountpartywarehouse.com.au](https://discountpartywarehouse.com.au/lollies/by-type/bulk/?utm_source=openai))\n\nQuick buying tips\n- Compare price per kg (or per-piece) including shipping — some “cheap” listings become pricey with freight. (Check each store’s product page for weight & delivery). ([costco.com.au](https://www.costco.com.au/SKITTLES/Skittles-Variety-Pack-60-Pack-900g/p/93134_BD?utm_source=openai))  \n- Check minimums / membership requirements (Costco often needs membership and has delivery/postcode restrictions). ([costco.com.au](https://www.costco.com.au/SKITTLES/Skittles-Variety-Pack-60-Pack-900g/p/93134_BD?utm_source=openai))  \n- If you’re serving at an outdoor event or need chocolate items, consider temperature and choose insulated shipping or local pickup.  \n- For school events or public distribution, check ingredient/allergen labelling and shelf-life on the supplier page.  \n- For very large or regular orders, ask wholesalers about trade pricing, samples and lead times.\n\nIf you tell me:\n- roughly how many kilos or how many party bags, and  \n- whether you want branded lollies (e.g., Allen’s/Skittles/Jellybeans) or unbranded/gourmet/sour/gummies — I can compare current per-kg prices & delivery for 3–4 of these sites and give a clear cheapest option for your exact needs."
